Yes.  But my list was less what I would consider ideal, but rather
what I consider almost the bare minimum for an ascension run, plus a
few items that are extremely useful if you can get them.  The wand of
digging might not be permanent, but it'll give you a few rounds of
instant relative safety when you see something like
"Orcus summons Demogorgon.
The soldier wields a cockatrice corpse. --more--
A voice booms out...
So thou thought thou couldst kill me, fool."

I'd certainly *like* to have a wand of fire in such cases; a wand of
death would be nice, too. But I'll make *sure* I have a wand of
digging before I go anywhere near somewhere that could happen.
And besides, you can engrave Elbereth multiple times with wands of
digging and still have charges to spare.  If you need to wait and
fight, just engrave 3 Elbereths and add a new one whenever one gets
damaged.


